    "90328003.2": "@?#$b#Can you wait a moment? I'm still on the phone. $7",
    "90328003.3": "Didn't you say that if I left, I shouldn't come back? Then why are you calling now? $5",
    "90328003.4": "And now you're asking me to go back and live with people I don't even know? Do you think I'm still a child? $5#$b#From the day I walked out your door, I chose my own life, and it has nothing to do with you anymore! $8",
    "90328003.5": "Uh, @? $3",
    "90328003.6": "So...? $7#$b#Did you hear all that? $3",
    "90328003.7": "#Can you tell me why you're so upset?#Please! Marry me!",
    "90328003.8": "Do I really need to explain? $3#$b#It's just... $3",
    "90328003.9": "My parents... $3#$b#They like to control everything about my life. $16",
    "90328003.10": "They're used to it, thinking that only when they're in control is everything right. $3#$b#But this time, I want to live my life my way.",
    "90328003.11": "I'll keep this between us.",
    "90328003.12": "I wish you all the best in life.",
    "90328003.13": "Can you be my daughter?",
    "90328003.14": "I don't think that's necessary. All my friends know my relationship with my family isn't good. $27#$b#So it's not exactly a secret. $26",
    "90328003.15": "Thanks? I guess... But since I got here, not much has gone smoothly. $17",
    "90328003.16": "Are you trying to control my life too? $7",
    "90328003.17": "So...? After all that, are you still interested in buying anything today? $19",
    "90328003.18": "Or? I have a raffle ticket here. Want to try your luck at the entrance? $22",
    "90328003_2.1": "What do you mean by that? $5#$b#Go away! I've got other things to do. $8",

    "90329001.1": "You are? Oh, the farmer from Pelican Town.",
    "90329001.2": "There used to be a lot of shops here, but some have closed down now. #$b#Have you ever thought about selling something? $1",
    "90329001.3": "My farm sells goods every day.",
    "90329001.4": "I've already started selling products.",
    "90329001.5": "I think selling in Pelican Town is enough for now.",
    "90329001.6": "Is that so? #$b#I forgot farmers also ship their own goods. $1",
    "90329001.7": "Really? #$b#Looks like I could source some of your farm's produce through Lewis.",
    "90329001.8": "Pelican Town might already be enough for you. #$b#But I think expanding a bit wouldn't hurt.",
    "90329001.9": "If you have time in the future, you could try renting a shop here. #$b#Though I'd need to prepare some materials for that.",
    "90329001.10": "But I think it might take a bit of time, don't you agree? $1",

    "90328004.1": "Who's there?",
    "90328004.2": "Oh, it's you. I thought it was someone else. $3",
    "90328004.3": "Are you okay?",
    "90328004.4": "Why do you look so pale?",
    "90328004.5": "What happened to your hair?",
    "90328004.6": "Oh? Uhh... I'm alright, I guess? $2#$b#I've already gotten used to this kind of life. $3",
    "90328004.7": "I think it might have to do with staying indoors too long. $2#$b#I don't know why, but being outside for too long makes me feel dizzy. $3",
    "90328004.8": "My hair? Do you think it's dyed? $29#$b#If I told you it's genetic, would you believe me? $3",
    "90328004.9": "As you guessed, my health isn't great. $3#$b#But it's not terrible either... at least not life-threatening. $17",
    "90328004.10": "The doctor said my condition is genetic. $7",
    "90328004.11": "Let's talk about something else, shall we? $19#$b#Have you ever thought about your future, @?",
    "90328004.12": "As for me... No. I haven't even hoped to see tomorrow's sunrise. $3#$b#Besides, I can't even handle today. $3",
    "90328004.13": "It's no big deal. Living each day is enough.",
    "90328004.14": "You should have faith in the future.",
    "90328004.15": "Maybe you should go out more often.",
    "90328004.16": "Just 'live' each day, huh? $2#$b#Like you, working hard for tomorrow? ",
    "90328004.17": "I wish I could do that. $7#$b#But most likely, it won't go the way I want. $3",
    "90328004.18": "No, I'd die out there. $3#$b#And it'd be an ugly death. $29",
    "90328004.19": "If there's a chance? $19#$b#Forget it. Dreams don't change anything. $7",
    "90328004.20": "It's nothing, just some things that don't need to be said out loud. $7#$b#That's it for today. I need to go back and rest. $3",

    "90328005.1": "It's this late already. Why aren't you here yet?$3#$b#Don't tell me I've been stood up again?$2",
    "90328005.2": "When did you get here?$9#$b#I thought I'd been abandoned again.$3",
    "90328005.3": "You know... about what happened last time.$7#$b#I just don't feel comfortable discussing things like that with someone I'm not really close to.$2",
    "90328005.4": "I've even made up my mind to live out my life alone, right here in this town.$29#$b#I used to think love was something I could never dream of.$9",
    "90328005.5": "I've never thought I'd make a good wife. I haven't even considered raising kids.$3#$b#I'm not sure if my issues would affect the next generation. Either way, I've never really liked kids.$2",
    "90328005.6": "Are you even listening to me?",
    "90328005.7": "What I like is you, not anything else.",
    "90328005.8": "You won't spend your life alone anymore.",
    "90328005.9": "Looks like we're the same kind of person.",
    "90328005.10": "I hope you're not lying to me.$2#$b#Because if you are, I'd still believe you like a fool.$9",
    "90328005.11": "Growing old together with you?$9#$b#Well, I do want to be with you.$22",
    "90328005.12": "Maybe?$17#$b#But I doubt anyone would want to be with someone like me.$2#$b#But you're different, aren't you?",
    "90328005.13": "So? I think it's better you know this now.$3#$b#I don't want to hide anything from the person I love, because you're the only one I trust now.$7",
    "90328005.14": "You understand what I'm saying, right?$14"
}